hey everyone its Johanna here burgers  hotdogs and french fries are just some  of our favorite fast foods according to  a recent article on Huffington Post  Americans eat nearly 50 billion burgers  a year and according to a survey done by  the national hot dog and sausage council  they estimate that Americans eat an  average of 20 billion hot dogs a year  and on top of that the average Americans  consume about 29 pounds of french fries  in a year taking in consideration that  all these surveys and research are only  based on Americans we as a whole consume  a lot more burgers hot dogs and french  fries worldwide hence that's why the  global fast food sales are projected to  reach 259 point seven billion dollars  this year while I do enjoy my occasional  fast foods they never leave me feeling  good afterwards  I tend to feel really bloated that's  because fast foods are high in sodium  sugar unhealthy fat high in calories and  there are no nutritional values  whatsoever so instead of avoiding them  we want to be making our own healthier  version of burgers hot dogs and french  fries let's go back to the basic of fast  foods and use minimal ingredients with  high nutritional values what I have here  is a store-bought veggie burger let's  take a look at the ingredients carrot  11% beans 6% wheat protein so I  concentrated stabilizer flavor and Hansa  color gelling agent right too many too  complicated to make a healthy and  delicious veggie burger you will only  need seven basic ingredients we  you can change and adapt according to  your own preference and taste the seven  ingredients are rolled oats choose your  beans either red beans black beans  chickpeas choose your vegetables either  carrots bell peppers spinach choose your  sauce sweet chili sauce tomato sauce or  barbecue sauce  choose your herbs or spice cumin chili  powder or even paprika and of course  onion and garlic to bring all the  flavors together to make my sweet chili  veggie burger the ingredients I have  chosen are 1/3 cup of rolled oats 1 can  of chickpeas rinsed and drained 1 medium  carrot grated 1 tablespoon of sweet  chilli sauce 1/2 a teaspoon of chili  powder 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin cut a cup  of onion diced 2 cloves of garlic minced  and season with salt and pepper the  first step is to place oats carrots  onions and garlic into the food  processor process until all the  ingredients are finely minced then add  the chickpeas and process until the  chickpeas are mashed and well blended  with all the mixtures finally add your  chosen sauce and spices and continue to  process transfer the mixture into a bowl  and stir well to make sure that all the  sources and spices are combined and all  the chickpeas are meshed next preheat  the oven to 180 degrees Celsius or 350  degree Fahrenheit  coats a baking tray with a little bit of  cooking spray using your hands divide  the mixture into six equal sized  portions roll them into balls and  flatten them to make sixth patties each  Patty should be about quarter to half of  an inch high place the patties on the  baking tray and bake for 30 minutes  after 15 minutes flip the patties over  and bake for the remaining 15 minutes  until the patties are lightly browned  and crispy on the outside all this  ingredients used are edible without  to bake them so if you want to store  your veggie burgers don't bake them  place them in a container and freeze  them up when you are ready to eat then  bake them this will last you up to six  months if you are not a big fan of oats  don't worry the oats are only used to  find all the ingredients together you  will not taste the oats at all instead  you will be adding more nutritional  values to your burger  each veggie burger only has 85 0.33  calories and I've serve mine with muffin  buns so pick your ingredients start to  experiment and make your own healthy  veggie burger do let me know your  version of healthy veggie burger in the  comments below most fast food hotdogs  are high in unhealthy fat hence being  high in calories as well  Mylene hotdog is low in fat and high in  protein the key is to choose extra lean  ground meat when you buy your ground  meat go for a 95% lean meat and 5% fats  here are two packs of minced meat one is  extra lean with 95 percent of lean meat  and only 5% of fat the value pack has 77  percent of needs with 23 percent of fat  the extra lean meat only has 128  calories per 100 gram as for the value  pack it has 276 calories per 100 gram  that's more than twice the amount of  calories that's because one gram of fat  has nine calories and one gram of  protein has four calories price  difference the extra lean meat is only  one pound more expensive so save your  waistline and save your health by  choosing extra lean meat the ingredients  you need to make my lean hotdogs are  quarter cup of rolled oats 250 gram of  extra lean means meat either pork turkey  the  a lamb or chicken one large egg white  lightly beaten two cloves of garlic  minced quarter cup of onion diced half a  teaspoon of dried mixed herbs half a  teaspoon of paprika and season with salt  and pepper the first step is to grind  the oats in a food processor and to find  and set it aside  then place the minced meat in the food  processor and process until very fine  add the oats egg white onion and garlic  and process until you have a paste  finally add the mix herbs paprika and  season with salt and pepper pulse the  mixture for another 30 seconds to  combine all the ingredients evenly  transfer the mixture into a bowl cover  and chill in the fridge for 45 minutes  to an hour once the mixture is chill  divide into five equal sized portions  shape and roll each portion between your  hands to form a four to five inches long  lock do not roll the hotdogs too thin  because without the casing they might  break apart when cooking  next place the hotdogs in a pan then add  enough water to cover almost halfway out  of the meat bring to a boil and then  reduce the heat to medium and simmer  gently turn the hotdogs occasionally  until they are thoroughly cook for about  15 minutes then remove and a lot of hot  dogs to cool down at this point you can  choose to bake or grill your hotdogs  like what I've done here and serve  immediately as for the remaining hotdogs  stall them in a container and keep them  in the fridge for up to two days or you  can freeze them up for up to six months  this hotdog is packed full of protein  extremely low in fat and each serving  has ninety three point four calories I  served it with multigrain roll and this  is a great post-workout meal  if you want to make hamburgers you can  use the exact same ingredients and just  make the paste into a burger like shape  I've also served a sign of the sweet  potato fries with both my veggie burger  and hot dogs french fries  one of the unhealthiest foods with high  amount of salt trans fat and calories  they are deep fried loaded with oil and  has no nutritional values whatsoever to  have a healthy side of fries let's  choose sweet potatoes instead and more  importantly to oven baked instead of  deep-frying to make a classic sweet  potato fries the ingredients you need  are 250 gram of sweet potatoes peeled  and cut into wedges 1 TSP of olive oil  1/2 a teaspoon of paprika and 1/2 a  teaspoon of cumin you may also choose  any other spices of your choice preheat  the oven to 200 degrees Celsius or 400  degree Fahrenheit in a bowl toss  together all the ingredients until  potatoes are evenly coated with oil and  spices then spread potatoes on a single  layer on the baking tray bake for a  total of 25 to 30 minutes after 15  minutes turn them over and return to the  oven and bake for another 10 to 15  minutes until they are well browned and  serve so the next time you're craving  for a fast food meal go into the kitchen  and make your own healthy fast food  instead these fast foods are high in  nutritional values and they taste even  better so be good to your body for new  Fitness food and motivational videos  please like share and subscribe to my  You Tube channel and website do you  follow me on Facebook Instagram and  Twitter to stay connected with me thanks  guys  Oh
 

